# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  apps/mobile — NOT a Vercel project
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Expo reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* from this file automatically. app.config.ts turns
#  it into extra.apiBaseUrl. Full guide: docs/MOBILE.md
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# LEAVE THIS COMMENTED to use the deployed API — that is app.config.ts's
# built-in fallback (https://apna-ghar-api.vercel.app/api), and it is what you
# want for a normal Expo Go test.
#
# Uncomment ONLY to point at an API running on your own machine. It must be
# your LAN address — `ipconfig`, the IPv4 line of your Wi-Fi adapter.
# NOT localhost and NOT 127.0.0.1: on a phone, those are the phone.
# Keep the /api suffix. Allow port 3000 through Windows Firewall the first time.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.42:3000/api

# Sign in with the seeded agent: 0300 1234567, code 123456
# (works while the API has OTP_DEV_MODE=true — the app prefills it for you).
